        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/super-yooka-laylee-kart-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>It's somehow been seven years since <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/yooka-laylee\">Yooka-Laylee</a>'s last proper adventure (I'm not sure 2025's remake, as <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/yooka-replaylee-brings-big-improvements-to-the-retro-throwback-but-loses-some-of-its-old-school-charm-along-the-way\">enjoyable as it was</a>, entirely counts), but the bat and lizard duo are finally back, and this time in a brand-new form. Yes, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/super-yooka-laylee-kart-leaks\">those recent leaks were right</a>: we're in for some classic SNES-style kart racing action when the now-officially announced Super Yooka-Laylee Kart arrives for PC at some currently undisclosed future time.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/super-yooka-laylee-kart-announced-playtonic\">Read more</a></p>",
